# Deny everything, then allow only what the build genuinely needs.
#
# An allowlist is used deliberately: a denylist silently admits anything the
# author forgot, and the thing most likely to be forgotten is the thing most
# dangerous to include. Nothing containing a credential, a key, or
# installation-specific trust material can reach the build context.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/

# Test fixtures are excluded: the image contains only the binary, and the feed
# used at run time is supplied as a read-only mount.
testdata/
keys/
secrets/
certs/
state/
logs/
data/
config/
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.log
.git/
